&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Reentry Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inversion is an aerospace and defense company pioneering advanced reentry technology to enable next-generation capabilities from space. By combining high-performance materials, precision aerodynamics, and mission-driven autonomy, Inversion is transforming reentry into an operational capability for an entirely new class of missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s highly maneuverable reentry spacecraft, Arc, is designed for rapid global cargo delivery, hypersonic testing, and other national security missions that require precise, controlled flight through the atmosphere. Arc creates an entirely new transportation domain, unlocking unprecedented speed and global reach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Los Angeles, Inversion designs, manufactures, and integrates its spacecraft under one roof, enabling the company to move rapidly from concept to flight. The company is backed by leading investors including Y Combinator, Spark Capital, and Lockheed Martin Ventures, with customers across the U.S. government and commercial space industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Avionics Embedded Software Engineering Intern, you will support the development, integration, verification, and debugging of embedded software for Inversion’s next-generation reentry vehicles. You will sit within the Avionics team and work closely with embedded software, electrical, RF, GNC, test, and vehicle engineers to develop software that interfaces directly with flight hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will gain hands-on experience developing and debugging firmware and embedded software, bringing up new hardware, integrating sensors and communications interfaces, and validating software in laboratory and hardware-in-the-loop environments. This is a practical, systems-focused internship for students interested in embedded systems, real-time software, flight computers, hardware/software integration, and aerospace applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with embedded software and avionics engineers to develop, integrate, test, and debug flight software and firmware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop software for microcontrollers, processors, sensors, communications interfaces, and other avionics hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support board bring-up and hardware/software integration, including debugging interfaces between embedded software and electrical hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and debug drivers and interfaces such as SPI, I2C, UART, CAN, Ethernet, GPIO, ADCs, and other embedded interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute software tests using laboratory hardware, engineering test fixtures, and hardware-in-the-loop systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support real-time software development using an RTOS or similar embedded software framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug software and hardware issues using tools such as oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, debuggers, serial consoles, and software instrumentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop test scripts and analysis tools using Python or similar languages to automate validation and characterize system behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integration of sensors, flight computers, RF systems, power electronics, and other avionics subsystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze failures and anomalies, identify root causes, and work with multidisciplinary teams to implement and verify corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document software behavior, test results, interfaces, and technical findings to support flight hardware development and verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be enrolled in a bachelor’s, master&#39;s or doctorate degree program in computer engineering, electrical engineering, computer science, aerospace engineering, or a related engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GPA of 3.0 or above.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ months of applied engineering experience (internship, laboratory, and personal/team project experience is applicable).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework or project experience in embedded systems, computer architecture, operating systems, real-time systems, or related disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience programming in C or C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing software for a microcontroller, embedded processor, FPGA-based system, robotics platform, or similar hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate technical results clearly to multidisciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with an RTOS such as Zephyr, FreeRTOS, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with embedded Linux or low-level software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing device drivers or low-level hardware interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SPI, I2C, UART, CAN, Ethernet, GPIO, ADCs, or similar embedded interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging embedded systems using oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, JTAG/SWD debuggers, or similar tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with board bring-up and hardware/software integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing automated software tests or hardware-in-the-loop test systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python for test automation, data analysis, or development tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with real-time concepts such as interrupts, scheduling, concurrency, synchronization, timing constraints, and memory management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing embedded systems through Formula SAE, student rocketry, CubeSat, robotics, or similar engineering projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous internship experience at a space, aerospace, or hardware startup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Git, CI/CD, software configuration management, and collaborative software development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our office headquarters is located in Playa Vista, CA. This position requires in-office presence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;The California annual base hourly rate for this role is currently $38-$41. Pay Grades are determined by role, level, location, and alignment with market data.&amp;nbsp; Individual pay will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: interviews and an assessment of several factors that are unique to each candidate, job-related skills, relevant education and experience, certifications, abilities of the candidate and internal equity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Inversion provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, veteran status, or disability.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Inversion collects and processes personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws.&amp;nbsp; If you are a US Job Applicant see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://oag.ca.gov/privacy/ccpa&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CCPA Privacy Policy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for further details.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Reentry Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inversion is an aerospace and defense company pioneering advanced reentry technology to enable next-generation capabilities from space. By combining high-performance materials, precision aerodynamics, and mission-driven autonomy, Inversion is transforming reentry into an operational capability for an entirely new class of missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s highly maneuverable reentry spacecraft, Arc, is designed for rapid global cargo delivery, hypersonic testing, and other national security missions that require precise, controlled flight through the atmosphere. Arc creates an entirely new transportation domain, unlocking unprecedented speed and global reach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Los Angeles, Inversion designs, manufactures, and integrates its spacecraft under one roof, enabling the company to move rapidly from concept to flight. The company is backed by leading investors including Y Combinator, Spark Capital, and Lockheed Martin Ventures, with customers across the U.S. government and commercial space industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;572&quot; data-local-id=&quot;4f74d2a13cf4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW6696791 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW6696791 BCX8&quot;&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;589&quot; data-local-id=&quot;5277259e656e&quot;&gt;As a Harness Design Engineer II on the Avionics team, you will contribute to harness design and integration activities from conceptual design to system integration – including component selection, process development, qualification, and production. By demonstrating proficiency in all phases of harness design, this interdisciplinary role offers growth opportunities and exposure to subsystem- and system-level design through collaboration with cross-disciplinary stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1128&quot; data-local-id=&quot;1864caf4fbf4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1155&quot; data-local-id=&quot;f269faa97c7c&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1283&quot; data-local-id=&quot;9dd667b39946&quot;&gt;Typically 2+ years of professional experience in wire harness design, electrical systems design, or hands on harness manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1409&quot; data-local-id=&quot;5ea3e936f950&quot;&gt;Ability to read/interpret electrical schematics and mechanical layout drawings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1492&quot; data-local-id=&quot;dcd4363d365f&quot;&gt;Understanding of wire gauge selection, current carrying capacity, and voltage drop calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1592&quot; data-local-id=&quot;b9d867f39589&quot;&gt;Proficiency with 3D CAD software (NX, CATIA, SolidWorks, or similar) for harness design and routing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1696&quot; data-local-id=&quot;ffc49f55200b&quot;&gt;Experience creating wiring diagrams, routing in 3D, and producing 2D drawings for production harnesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1803&quot; data-local-id=&quot;74f1ed1809b1&quot;&gt;Ability to generate and maintain accurate technical documentation in accordance with engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1914&quot; data-local-id=&quot;3fdcce3e0a31&quot;&gt;Strong communication skills with the ability to present technical work at design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2007&quot; data-local-id=&quot;fc388b35c0d2&quot;&gt;Ability to work collaboratively with multidisciplinary teams and manufacturing/integration personnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2007&quot; data-local-id=&quot;fc388b35c0d2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must have the ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. government Secret/Top Secret security clearance.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2112&quot; data-local-id=&quot;a3f464e4856f&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2140&quot; data-local-id=&quot;781f88d20f82&quot;&gt;Experience with aerospace, defense, or spacecraft electrical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2213&quot; data-local-id=&quot;585f167ee7e2&quot;&gt;Experience with NX CAD software specifically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2262&quot; data-local-id=&quot;84e044b4c2cf&quot;&gt;Hands-on experience with development and test harness design for qualification testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2353&quot; data-local-id=&quot;671aced31e3c&quot;&gt;Experience developing or contributing to Interface Control Documents (ICDs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2433&quot; data-local-id=&quot;c4153df827ba&quot;&gt;Experience designing harness mounts, brackets, and secondary structures.&lt;/li&gt;
