&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will focus on&amp;nbsp;identifying, qualifying, pursuing,&amp;nbsp;and capturing hypersonic flight tests and targets in support of the USG and industry partner needs.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;You will work closely with the leadership team across BD, Engineering, Missions, and Contracts&amp;nbsp;to provide best value and executable flight tests to buying customers.&amp;nbsp;Responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and engage new customers via phone, email, LinkedIn, and in-person outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the company at aerospace and defense trade shows, conferences, and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualify inbound and outbound leads and convert them into active sales opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct introductory calls and meetings to understand customer needs and align them with our hypersonic capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a pipeline of qualified opportunities in CRM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with engineering and leadership to support technical discussions and proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track market activity, competitor positioning, and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support early capture activities for government and defense programs (as applicable).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically 10+ years in one or more of the following:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall technical sales leadership for hypersonic capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Procuring hypersonic flight tests and/or targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly managing hypersonic flight experiments or target exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a technical sales role for commercial or government&amp;nbsp;for hypersonic&amp;nbsp;capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with high-volume outbound calling and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging technical and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with the ability to translate complex technical concepts into customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for trade shows and customer meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must have the ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. government Secret/Top Secret security clearance.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aerospace engineering or technical background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the various hypersonic flight test modalities and targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the various current options for hypersonic flight tests and targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of various test options for hypersonic systems, subsystems, and components, including via wind tunnel testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of various hypersonic target options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with government customers, commercial customers, and stakeholders for hypersonic tests and/or targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active DoD security clearance. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our office headquarters is located in Playa Vista, CA. This position requires in office presence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
