&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Reentry Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inversion is an aerospace and defense company pioneering advanced reentry technology to enable next-generation capabilities from space. By combining high-performance materials, precision aerodynamics, and mission-driven autonomy, Inversion is transforming reentry into an operational capability for an entirely new class of missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s highly maneuverable reentry spacecraft, Arc, is designed for rapid global cargo delivery, hypersonic testing, and other national security missions that require precise, controlled flight through the atmosphere. Arc creates an entirely new transportation domain, unlocking unprecedented speed and global reach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Los Angeles, Inversion designs, manufactures, and integrates its spacecraft under one roof, enabling the company to move rapidly from concept to flight. The company is backed by leading investors including Y Combinator, Spark Capital, and Lockheed Martin Ventures, with customers across the U.S. government and commercial space industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The Government Relations Executive will lead the company’s congressional engagement and federal government relations strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We are open to considering candidates at the Director, Senior Director, or Vice President level. Final leveling will be based on the candidate’s experience, demonstrated scope and impact, depth of relevant relationships, leadership experience, and other applicable compensable factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This executive will serve as a trusted advisor to the senior leadership team on congressional priorities, defense authorization and appropriations, acquisition policy, federal budgets, and the political and programmatic factors affecting the company’s strategic objectives. The successful candidate will develop and execute integrated legislative strategies that protect and expand existing programs, support new business opportunities, shape relevant policy, and strengthen the company’s position within the national security community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate will bring extensive, senior-level experience working in both chambers of Congress, including positions supporting the Senate Armed Services Committee and House Armed Services Committee. The candidate should possess deep relationships with congressional members and staff, Department of Defense leaders, military-service acquisition organizations, and other stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and lead the company’s comprehensive federal government relations and congressional engagement strategy in alignment with corporate growth objectives and program priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise the CEO, executive leadership team, business-unit leaders, and program executives on congressional developments, defense budgets, acquisition policy, political dynamics, and legislative opportunities and risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute legislative strategies supporting interceptors, integrated air and missile defense, hypersonic systems, and other advanced national security capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain trusted relationships with members of Congress, professional and personal committee staff, congressional leadership, defense appropriators, relevant congressional delegations, and other key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engagement with the Senate Armed Services Committee, House Armed Services Committee, Senate and House Appropriations Committees, congressional leadership offices, and relevant member offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor, assess, and shape the National Defense Authorization Act, defense appropriations legislation, supplemental appropriations, committee reports, authorization and appropriations marks, and other legislation affecting the company’s programs and markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strategies to secure program authorizations, appropriations, congressional funding increases, supportive report language, policy provisions, and other legislative outcomes consistent with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and address legislative or regulatory barriers affecting defense acquisition, testing, production, contracting, industrial-base capacity, program execution, and the transition of emerging technologies into programs of record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technical, operational, acquisition, and budget matters into clear and compelling messages for congressional and executive-branch audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide timely intelligence and actionable analysis concerning congressional priorities, program funding, acquisition strategies, oversight concerns, competitive positioning, and potential changes in defense policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with business development, strategy, program management, finance, communications, legal, contracts, and engineering teams to ensure consistent government engagement and advocacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare senior company leaders for congressional meetings, hearings, briefings, site visits, industry engagements, and other interactions with government stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the company in meetings with members of Congress, congressional staff, Department of Defense officials, military-service leaders, industry associations, and other national security stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop congressional engagement strategies that communicate the operational value, technological maturity, industrial-base contribution, and economic impact of company programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize congressional delegation visits, facility tours, supplier-network engagements, employee advocacy initiatives, and other events that demonstrate program and workforce impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build coalitions with customers, suppliers, industry partners, trade associations, and other stakeholders in support of shared legislative and policy objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish measurable government relations objectives, track progress against those objectives, and regularly brief executive leadership on results, emerging issues, and recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and mentor government relations personnel and effectively manage external consultants and other advocacy resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all government relations activities comply with applicable lobbying, ethics, campaign-finance, disclosure, and corporate compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in political science, public policy, national security, business, engineering, law, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Typically 12 years of progressively responsible experience in Congress, the executive branch, the defense industry, or a combination of these environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant professional experience supporting both the Senate and the House of Representatives, including service in positions supporting the Senate Armed Services Committee and House Armed Services Committee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience working on interceptors, hypersonic, integrated air and missile defense, or closely related defense programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the congressional authorization and appropriations processes, including the National Defense Authorization Act and annual defense appropriations legislation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of Department of Defense planning, programming, budgeting, and execution; defense acquisition processes; program oversight; and the congressional budget cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with relevant congressional committees, member offices, congressional leadership, the Department of Defense, military services, and defense acquisition organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated record of developing and executing legislative strategies that produced measurable funding, policy, acquisition, or program outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical and programmatic issues and communicate them effectively to both specialist and nontechnical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising C-suite executives and other senior leaders on sensitive legislative, political, budgetary, and business matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives involving government relations, business development, program management, finance, legal, contracts, communications, and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional judgment, discretion, integrity, written communication, public-speaking, negotiation, and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced environment, manage competing priorities, and respond rapidly to legislative and program developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;Must have the ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. government Secret/Top Secret security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior service as professional staff, military legislative assistant, counsel, or senior advisor to the Senate Armed Services Committee or House Armed Services Committee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting both congressional Armed Services Committees during the development of defense authorization legislation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the Senate or House Appropriations Committee, particularly its Defense Subcommittee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive-branch experience within the Office of the Secretary of War, Department of the Army, Department of the Navy, Department of the Air Force, Department of the Space Force, Missile Defense Agency, or another defense acquisition organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with one or more major mission areas, including hypersonic weapons, missile warning, command and control, integrated air and missile defense, homeland missile defense, or advanced interceptors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of relevant acquisition organizations, program executive offices, combatant commands, test organizations, and defense industrial-base stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing congressional funding increases, influencing authorization or appropriations language, addressing acquisition-policy barriers, or supporting the transition of advanced technology into operational programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a corporate government relations or legislative affairs organization and managing external lobbying firms, consultants, political engagement activities, and compliance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graduate degree in public policy, national security, business administration, law, engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret or Top Secret/Sensitive Compartmented Information security clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Leveling &amp;amp; Compensation:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This position may be hired at the&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Director, Senior Director, or Vice President level depending on the candidate’s experience, qualifications, demonstrated impact, and the scope of responsibility they are positioned to assume.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anticipated Base Salary Ranges:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Director: $180,000 to $275,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior Director: $215,000 to $310,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vice President: $245,000 to $350,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;In addition to base salary, this position is eligible for equity, bonus or incentive compensation, and other benefits in accordance with the company’s applicable compensation programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Final title, level, and compensation will be determined based on applicable compensable factors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;sub&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Washington D.C. annual base salary for this role is currently $180,000 - $350,000.&amp;nbsp; Pay Grades are determined by role, level, location, and alignment with market data. Individual pay will be determined on a case-by-case basis and may vary based on the following considerations: interviews and an assessment of several factors that are unique to each candidate, job-related skills, relevant education and experience, certifications, abilities of the candidate and internal equity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ITAR Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;To conform to U.S. Government space technology export regulations, including the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) you must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Inversion provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, veteran status, or disability.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;Inversion collects and processes personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws.&amp;nbsp; If you are a US Job Applicant see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://oag.ca.gov/privacy/ccpa&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CCPA Privacy Policy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for further details.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Reentry Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inversion is an aerospace and defense company pioneering advanced reentry technology to enable next-generation capabilities from space. By combining high-performance materials, precision aerodynamics, and mission-driven autonomy, Inversion is transforming reentry into an operational capability for an entirely new class of missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company’s highly maneuverable reentry spacecraft, Arc, is designed for rapid global cargo delivery, hypersonic testing, and other national security missions that require precise, controlled flight through the atmosphere. Arc creates an entirely new transportation domain, unlocking unprecedented speed and global reach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Los Angeles, Inversion designs, manufactures, and integrates its spacecraft under one roof, enabling the company to move rapidly from concept to flight. The company is backed by leading investors including Y Combinator, Spark Capital, and Lockheed Martin Ventures, with customers across the U.S. government and commercial space industry.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW6696791 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW6696791 BCX8&quot;&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;As&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Ground Software Engineer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt; at Inversion &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;you will build, integrate, and test the mission control software, real-time telemetry processing pipelines, and data visualization tools required to operate and monitor the Arc vehicle. You will own the development of user interfaces and backend applications u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;sed in both test and operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Design, develop, and maintain the backend architectures, telemetry parsers, and command pipelines that support ground operations and flight tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Build highly reliable, low-latency operator displays and data visualization interfaces used during vehicle testing and missions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Develop, package, and deploy automated software tools to orchestrate and monitor Hardware-in-the-Loop (HIL) and Software-in-the-Loop (SIL) simulation runs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Define and implement communication protocol structures, serialization standards, and data definitions (e.g., JSON, Protobuf, YAML) between flight and ground hardware.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Build and maintain high-rate time-series databases and data storage solutions for rapid post-test analysis and archive searching.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Integrate ground station software interfaces to manage uplink and downlink RF hardware, tracking antennas, and network routing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Provide direct, real-time software support during integrated vehicle testing, troubleshooting networking or command-and-control drops.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or equivalent technical experience.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Typically 2+ years of professional experience developing software, with a focus on ground control systems, telemetry pipelines, or distributed systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Proficiency in&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Rust&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;a Linux environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;working with network communication protocols (such as TCP, UDP, and WebSockets).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to coordinate across software and hardware teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;Must have the ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. government Secret/Top Secret security clearance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Desired Qualifications:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Experience working in full-stack software development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Familiarity with existing aerospace mission control and ground software frameworks (such as COSMOS, Open MCT, Yamcs, or similar).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Experience with containerization (Docker, Kubernetes) and modern DevOps practices (GitLab CI, GitHub Actions).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Familiarity with RF communication systems, satellite link characteristics, or digital signal processing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;Normal (Web)&quot;&gt;Prior experience working in startups and/or small independent engineering teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our office headquarters is located in Playa Vista, CA. This position requires in office presence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
